# ---- Publication content: kept on this machine, not on the public repository ----
# The public repo now carries only the tool (the app, its source, its tests) so that an evaluator
# can run it without anything about the unpublished manuscript being visible. Every path below
# still exists in full on disk; git simply stops tracking it. Removed from every past commit too,
# via git filter-repo, on 2026-09-20.
#
# Every rule below is ANCHORED with a leading slash. Unanchored, a bare name matches a directory
# of that name at ANY depth, and two of these were doing real damage: 'figures/' also matched
# src/sai_cns/figures/ and 'docs/' matched src/sai_cns/docs/, so a NEW source file in either would
# have been silently untracked and would never have reached the public repository. The 18 scripts
# already in src/sai_cns/figures/ survived only because ignore rules do not apply to files git
# already tracks, which is luck rather than design. Anchoring removes the trap.
#
# manuscript_nar_clean/ and comments/ are new here. They were matched by NO rule at all, so both
# finished manuscripts, the cover letter and the reviewer comments would have been published by
# any `git add -A`.
/manuscript/
/manuscript_nar_clean/
/comments/
/docs/
/thesis/
/presentation/
/supplementary/
/figures/
/AUDIT_PACKAGE/
/archive/
/reviewer_package/
/validation/
/data/
/audit/
/repro/
#
# results/ and inversion/ stay out, with one deliberate exception: the handful of small tables the
# SERVED INTERFACE reads. Without them the landing page degrades silently rather than failing. It
# rendered "- molecular targets" instead of "54", and /version returned an empty knowledge-graph
# fingerprint, because every read is guarded and the guard substitutes a placeholder. A public
# repository whose front page cannot render its own numbers is not self-sufficient, and the
# degradation is invisible to whoever deploys it. Seven files, about 35 KB.
/results/*
!/results/tables/
/results/tables/*
!/results/tables/MODEL_INVENTORY.csv
!/results/tables/inversion_validation.csv
!/results/tables/model_comparison.csv
!/results/tables/noncns_specificity_summary.csv
!/results/tables/rf_cv_summary.csv
!/results/tables/rf_temporal.csv
/inversion/*
!/inversion/results/
/inversion/results/*
!/inversion/results/GRAPH_FINGERPRINT.json

# ---- Internal bookkeeping: kept on this machine, not on the public repository ----
# None of these is needed to run the server or to reproduce the models. They are inventories of
# this working tree, which is not what an evaluator is being asked to evaluate, and the archive
# inventory in particular indexes superseded material that is deliberately not published.
/ARCHIVE_MANIFEST.csv
/REPOSITORY_INVENTORY.csv
/SCRIPT_INDEX.csv
/.regen_backup_path
